Z||000000||Jim Keyton||04-14-2001||08:17 AM||||I have an 88 with the stock radio. A while back the right rear speaker started a random popping. A little latter I replaced all four speakers, and the popping in the right rear continued. Just the other day I was parked just waiting for the wife and turned the key to accy to listen to the radio, and the right rear was popping, the same as when the car was running. Any ideas on what is causing this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||04-14-2001||08:25 AM||||I would say a bad speaker, but you said that you replacd them. It could be a loose wire. What type of speakers did you put in? They may also be bad.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-14-2001||08:58 AM||||Does the speaker "pop" when you turn the volume, fade, or balance? <BR>The controls over time can get dirty and cause that. If it is the controls, You could clean them with "TV Tuner cleaner" spray. (the radio has yo be removed and opened.) If it happens while just listening it could be a loose wire or connector. Even a dirty connector can cause it.<BR>At worse it could be the stock radio is going bad. I would check the above first.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-14-2001||03:47 PM||||read my cave artilce about the radio's.<P>try reaching behind the driver's side of the pod and wiggle the connector when it's doing it. ||||reg||1
